# Donor acknowledgment. The signatory is deliberately empty: no name is
# invented and no signature image is composited, so until the owner sets
# one the certificate prints a clear rule to sign by hand. Pub. 1771 does
# not require a signature, so an unsigned acknowledgment is still valid.
# Collective signatory by owner decision 2026-08-03. The owner needs to remain
# anonymous, so no individual is named. Pub. 1771 does not require a signature
# at all, so a collective attribution is fully valid at filing time. The title
# is plural to agree with the name, and deliberately does not repeat the
# organisation name, which already appears directly above it and again in the
# static "AUTHORIZED SIGNATURE FOR WIN'S VPN INC." rule beneath.
DONOR_ACK_SIGNATORY_NAME_DEFAULT="Directors of Win's VPN Inc."
DONOR_ACK_SIGNATORY_TITLE_DEFAULT="Authorized Officers"
# Footer contact. Empty falls back to "winsvpn.org | <EMAIL_SENDER>".
