# --- Litestream durability barrier (HANDOFF 3j) -----------------------------
# RPO 0 for the writes the hub gates on the barrier, and ONLY those: prepaid
# redemption and its acknowledgement, admin redemption batch issue and revoke,
# and the redemption, donor-acknowledgement and Hoppy agent mail outbox drains.
# For those the hub does not acknowledge until `litestream sync -wait -json`
# confirms the write replicated. NOT covered (IA-CP-17): PayPal, BTCPay and
# Monero grants and /verify device admissions are acknowledged after the local
# SQLite commit, so their RPO is Litestream's asynchronous replication lag, not
# 0. Extending the barrier to them is a hub behaviour change (a replication
# stall would then 503 payment webhooks and every connect) and is left to a
# separate ruling. The version is pinned here and the archive checksum is
# verified before install. An unverified binary is not a durability control.
#
# MINIMUM VERSION IS NOT COSMETIC. `sync -wait` first exists in 0.5.9 and the
# `-json` output the pinned parser reads first exists in 0.5.12. The previous
# pin here was 0.5.0, which has NEITHER -- the barrier could not have worked at
# all, it would only ever have failed closed. Do not lower this pin.
#
# The digests below are the published SHA-256 for the two Linux server
# architectures of this exact release, taken from the GitHub release asset
# digests (checksums.txt lists the same files). Any change of version REQUIRES
# changing both digests in the same edit.
LITESTREAM_VERSION_DEFAULT="${LITESTREAM_VERSION:-0.5.17}"
LITESTREAM_SHA256_AMD64_DEFAULT="${LITESTREAM_SHA256_AMD64:-cfb371176d164437ae869f8351cfde49bd1804ae71c61923f75c9cba9c9c006d}"
LITESTREAM_SHA256_ARM64_DEFAULT="${LITESTREAM_SHA256_ARM64:-f8ca4a050095c1efbda2c4365172e61bf9d955ea0d9ac42f448b52e51819baa5}"
LITESTREAM_DOWNLOAD_BASE_DEFAULT="${LITESTREAM_DOWNLOAD_BASE:-https://github.com/benbjohnson/litestream/releases/download}"
LITESTREAM_BIN_DEFAULT="${LITESTREAM_BIN:-/usr/local/bin/litestream}"
# FX-CP-A: write_env and the postflight barrier check both read this, but it
# was never defined, so under `set -u` write_env aborted with "unbound
# variable" whenever LITESTREAM_SYNC_TIMEOUT_SECONDS was not supplied. 30 is
# the hub's own default (main.py LITESTREAM_SYNC_TIMEOUT_SECONDS).
LITESTREAM_SYNC_TIMEOUT_SECONDS_DEFAULT="${LITESTREAM_SYNC_TIMEOUT_SECONDS:-30}"
LITESTREAM_REPLICA_URL_DEFAULT="${LITESTREAM_REPLICA_URL:-}"
# LSR (2026-10-02): the replica must take every gated write OFF this host. The
# earlier default was a directory on the hub's own disk, which let the barrier
# confirm a copy that one disk failure loses, and the gs:// replica depended on
# a Google Cloud project that was later disabled. The only replica accepted
# while DURABILITY_BARRIER_REQUIRED=1 is now Litestream's SFTP replica on an
# owner-controlled host, with that host's SSH key pinned:
#   LITESTREAM_REPLICA_URL=sftp://<user>@<host>[:<port>]/<absolute path>
#   LITESTREAM_SFTP_HOST_KEY="<type> <base64>"  (the receiver's sshd host key)
#   LITESTREAM_SFTP_KEY_PATH                    (client key; generated if absent)
# For aicore (no inbound route from the hub) the URL host is 127.0.0.1 and the
# port is the loopback listener of aicore's outbound reverse forward. Setting
# LITESTREAM_SFTP_TUNNEL_PUBLIC_KEY to aicore's tunnel public key authorises
# that forward on this hub for exactly that one listen port.
LITESTREAM_SFTP_KEY_PATH_DEFAULT="${LITESTREAM_SFTP_KEY_PATH:-/root/.ssh/wins_litestream_ed25519}"
LITESTREAM_SFTP_HOST_KEY_DEFAULT="${LITESTREAM_SFTP_HOST_KEY:-}"
LITESTREAM_SFTP_TUNNEL_PUBLIC_KEY_DEFAULT="${LITESTREAM_SFTP_TUNNEL_PUBLIC_KEY:-}"
LITESTREAM_SFTP_TUNNEL_USER_DEFAULT="${LITESTREAM_SFTP_TUNNEL_USER:-wins-replica-tunnel}"
DURABILITY_BARRIER_ENABLED_DEFAULT="${DURABILITY_BARRIER_ENABLED:-1}"
DURABILITY_BARRIER_REQUIRED_DEFAULT="${DURABILITY_BARRIER_REQUIRED:-1}"
DOUBLE_VPN_ENABLED_DEFAULT="${DOUBLE_VPN_ENABLED:-1}"
# D5: free sessions are capped on v3 and v1 at the data plane, and the Core carries the
