# Account deletion consent quorum (Apple Guideline 5.1.1(v) in-app deletion).
# A deletion must be confirmed from ACCOUNT_DELETION_QUORUM *distinct* active
# devices, so one stolen or compromised device can never destroy an account by
# itself. It is deliberately NOT DEVICE_LIMIT: requiring every slot would lock
# out any user whose device is lost, broken, or wiped, which Apple rejects as
# unreasonably burdensome. The effective threshold is always
# min(ACCOUNT_DELETION_QUORUM, live active-device count) computed at request
# time -- see required_deletion_confirmations -- so changing DEVICE_LIMIT never
# silently changes who is able to delete an account.
ACCOUNT_DELETION_QUORUM = max(1, int(os.getenv("ACCOUNT_DELETION_QUORUM", "2")))
# An account with exactly one active device cannot reach a two-device quorum,
# so it takes a time-delayed path instead: the single device confirms, the
# account sits in pending deletion for this long, and ANY device that signs in
# can cancel. That keeps the anti-theft property (a thief holding the only
# device cannot delete instantly, and the real owner has a window to activate a
# replacement and intervene) while guaranteeing every user can eventually
# delete. Seven days: long enough for an owner to notice a theft and act, far
# shorter than the 30-day grace period used by the major platforms, and it asks
# nothing further of the user once requested.
