def render_legal_document(company_identity: str) -> str:
    return f"""Win's VPN legal terms version {LEGAL_DOCUMENT_VERSION}, effective {LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE}.

OWNER APPROVED 2026-08-31; COUNSEL REVIEW PENDING. This marking does not state or imply that counsel reviewed these terms.

{company_identity}

Terms of service. Win's VPN is provided as a privacy, cybersecurity, and anti-censorship technology service using Winn Protocol. Availability, speed, routing, compatibility, server locations, and payment features may vary by region, network, censorship conditions, device, platform, and maintenance status. By activating or using Win's VPN, the customer agrees to use the service lawfully, not attack or abuse the service or infrastructure, and accept these terms, the hold harmless agreement, the limitation of liability, and electronic records consent.

Payment and refund policy. The 1 Month and 1 Year plans are recurring PayPal subscriptions charged at the interval shown until canceled. Cancel in PayPal before the next billing date to stop future payments. Canceling partway through a period already paid for ends access when PayPal reports the cancellation, not at the end of that period, and the unused part is not refunded. Purchases and redemptions are final and non-refundable to the maximum extent permitted by law, without limiting non-waivable legal or PayPal buyer-protection rights. A full refund, chargeback, or reversal may end access; a partial refund does not automatically end it. Full terms: https://www.winsvpn.org/billing/.

Acceptable use. The service must not be used for unlawful activity, abuse, harassment, intrusion, spam, malware, copyright infringement, torrenting, attacks against Win's VPN or third-party infrastructure, evasion of payment or device limits, credential sharing abuse, or activity that harms third parties or infrastructure. Win's VPN may suspend access, preserve evidence, cooperate with lawful process when required, and seek recovery of damages, costs, and fees caused by misuse, abuse, attacks, or unlawful conduct.

Free and sponsored access. Free access, trial access, donated access, and administrator-granted premium access are offered as discretionary, non-paid, revocable access. To the maximum extent permitted by law, users of free, trial, donated, or administrator-granted access agree that they receive the service without paid-service remedies, waive claims against Win's VPN Inc. and Win Empire LLC arising from that discretionary access, and remain fully responsible for their own conduct, misuse, local-law compliance, and third-party claims.

Privacy and Verified No Log policy. Before the user accepts the bundled Privacy Policy, the app uses only protected local settings needed to remember that choice and does not read a device hardware identifier, retrieve coarse public-IP location, fetch nodes or other network data, run tunnel or speed-test smoke checks, or request battery-optimization changes. After acceptance, the app sends a random app-install identifier generated on the device as a Device or other ID with device model, platform, app version, locale, account or free-access identity, selected location, and capability flags. That identifier is created locally and is not derived from a device hardware identifier or an advertising identifier; on Android, Windows, and Linux it is kept in the app's private storage and reinstalling produces a new one, and on Apple platforms it is kept in the device keychain and can survive a reinstall on the same device. The identifier may be account-linked for account management, the three-device limit, security, fraud prevention, and abuse prevention; it is not used for ads or tracking, sold, or shared for advertising. Win's VPN does not collect or keep VPN activity logs and does not log browsing history, DNS query history, traffic contents, raw VPN traffic, or user destination activity. Free-access verification and sign-out create a 30-day event containing the shared free identity, device and source-IP buckets, device public-key fingerprint, platform and device model, selected gateway, stealth choice, a user-agent hash, and time. It records that a free connection happened and which gateway served it, never what was done through it; paid accounts do not generate these events. \"Verified No Log\" is Win's VPN's name for these commitments and has not been independently audited or attested as of this version. Selected split-tunneling package identifiers stay in protected local settings and are passed locally to the operating-system VPN service; the full installed-app inventory is not uploaded. So that the app can still reach a working gateway when the usual DNS or CDN paths are censored, it also requests a small gateway-recovery file hosted on GitHub at raw.githubusercontent.com; GitHub necessarily receives the connection IP and ordinary request metadata for that request, the file only selects among gateways already built into the signed app, and no account number, device identifier, or other user data is sent with it. Only after the user requests the approximate-location map, before the VPN connects, the app asks first-party Win's VPN origins and gateways for an IP-derived scene and uses Cloudflare's speed.cloudflare.com/meta as the final fallback. Those services receive the pre-VPN connection IP. Apple Maps receives the region and connection IP on Apple platforms; a first-party Win's VPN endpoint serves OpenStreetMap-derived tiles on other platforms; Win's VPN does not request device GPS for this feature or retain the returned IP, city, postal code, or map-view history. While the app is disconnected, it may query the third-party service api.ipify.org to display the device's current public IP address next to the connection status indicator; that service receives the connection IP and ordinary request metadata for each such request, and no account number, device identifier, or other app data is sent, and the request is never made while a VPN tunnel is active. The app also generates a long-lived cryptographic key pair on first use of each account and derives a public key from it, transmitting that public key to Win's VPN with every account verification and configuration renewal request as a long-lived linkable device identifier for connection provisioning, the three-device limit, and abuse prevention; it is not derived from hardware or advertising identifiers, and the account-side record is deleted or overwritten when the device is deactivated, replaced, or no longer needed. When the user runs the in-app speed test, the app measures throughput against speed.cloudflare.com and cachefly.cachefly.net for every region, and, for nodes in the western United States, losangeles.ca.speedtest.frontier.com, lsanca-speedtest-ookla-02.st.charter.com, and speedtest.lax2.sonic.net; each receives the connection IP, ordinary request metadata, and the transferred measurement traffic, with no account number, device identifier, or other app data included, and only while the test is running. PayPal processes payment details and sends payment confirmation metadata, SMTP2GO processes transactional email, and hosting, CDN, security, app-store, and platform providers process the minimum data needed for their functions. To throttle repeated failed attempts and protect accounts, gateways, and infrastructure, the service keeps short-lived request counters and security-event records keyed to a hashed form of the source IP address, device identifier, or account number rather than to the address itself; those records exist only for security, fraud prevention, abuse response, and device-limit enforcement, are not used to profile a user or for advertising, and never contain VPN traffic, browsing history, DNS queries, or destination activity. If an account is created through a referral link, the referring account is recorded against the referred account so the account-validity bonus can be granted and reversed if the funding payment is refunded or cancelled. Transient connection/session state is cleared when the VPN disconnects. Device-limit metadata is deleted or overwritten when the device is deactivated, replaced, or no longer needed for active account operation, and app-collected operational data that is no longer needed is deleted or anonymized within 90 days. Account, payment, referral, and legal acceptance records are retained only while needed to operate the account, satisfy accounting/legal obligations, prevent fraud or abuse, resolve disputes, or document customer acceptance. Privacy access, correction, and deletion requests may be sent to privacy@winsvpn.org or support@winsvpn.org.

Camouflage safety mode. Android and iOS launcher icon camouflage and Android/iOS in-app calculator camouflage are user-safety features for high-risk censorship environments, including Burma/Myanmar, where a visible VPN interface can expose users to retaliation. On Android and iOS both are applied automatically once a device is activated and cannot be switched off in the app; the real interface is shown after the PIN is entered. Android TV and desktop builds have neither. They do not hide malicious activity, iOS may display an operating-system confirmation when changing the icon, and the operating system's VPN status remains visible while a tunnel is active.

